---
description: Extract distinct UI into named components. Compose parents from children.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Composable UI

Prefer small named components over packing several pieces into one parent. If a block has its own job (search, add, header chrome), give it a file and a name. Parents compose. They do not own the internals of their children.

```tsx
// BAD
export function WorkspaceShell() {
  return (
    <header>
      <input placeholder="Search workspace" />
      <button>Quick add</button>
      <UserAvatar />
    </header>
  );
}

// GOOD
export function WorkspaceHeader() {
  return (
    <header>
      <SearchWorkspace />
      <QuickAdd />
      <UserAvatar />
    </header>
  );
}
```

Do this even when the child is still a stub. We will grow it in place.

## Place files deliberately

Before creating or moving a file, decide which product area owns it. Keep
workspace-wide layout primitives in `components/layout`, and place
feature-specific components under their domain, such as
`components/wedding/overview`. Keep a component, its focused tests, and closely
related subcomponents together.

When a component's responsibility changes, revisit its location. Do not leave
feature code in a generic folder just because it started there.
